<title>COTE D'IVOIRE: Ivorian cocoa product exports rise in November.</title>
<headline>Ivorian cocoa product exports rise in November.</headline>
<dateline>ABIDJAN 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ivory Coast exported 8,778 tonnes of semi-finished cocoa products and powder in November against 7,061 tonnes in October, official shipping data show.</p>
<p>Cocoa product exports in November 1995 were 4,514 tonnes.</p>
<p>The data do not separate liquor, butter and cake shipments.</p>
<p>Product shipments from Abidjan totalled 7,328 tonnes, including 581 tonnes of powder, whereas San Pedro shipped 1,450 tonnes of cocoa products shown grouped together as one category.</p>
<p>Powder shipments from Abidjan totalled 660 tonnes in 1995/96.</p>
<p>Cumulative liquor, butter and cake shipments in the first two months of the 1996/97 (Oct-Sept) were 15,839 tonnes against 8,197 tonnes in the same period of 1995/96.</p>
<p>Exports in November 1995 were slowed by a freight rate dispute.</p>
<p>--Matthew Bunce, Abidjan Newsroom +225 21 90 90</p>
